1
00:00:01,640 --> 00:00:05,140
Come on, everyone. Cheers!

2
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:12,740
Alright, everyone.

3
00:00:12,740 --> 00:00:16,860
Listen up! Today is such an auspicious day

4
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:20,400
for us to throw a welcome party for my intern.

5
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:23,940
Jomkaen, sweetie, I'm so sorry.

6
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:25,900
This party is a whole month late.

7
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:29,900
But I welcome you with all my heart!

8
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:32,980
It's totally fine, P'Som-O. Thank you so much.

9
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:39,020
Throughout the past month, Jomkaen has done an amazing job.

10
00:00:39,020 --> 00:00:43,000
Truly, you've helped us out so much.

11
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:44,660
How could we not praise her?

12
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:48,660
The two of you dumped all your work on her!

13
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:51,180
Making her work like a workhorse.

14
00:00:51,180 --> 00:00:52,960
Why don't you look at the other department?

15
00:00:53,480 --> 00:00:55,400
Their intern, on the other hand,

16
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:58,660
has been chilling for weeks.

17
00:00:59,340 --> 00:01:01,380
Is that really okay, P'Best?

18
00:01:01,380 --> 00:01:03,780
Is it really?

19
00:01:05,220 --> 00:01:07,800
Well, honestly, it depends on the mentor.

20
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:10,560
If they've taught enough and logged enough hours,

21
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:12,660
I can't really complain.

22
00:01:12,980 --> 00:01:16,720
And who is Pond's mentor?

23
00:01:17,240 --> 00:01:19,940
It's... / It's...

24
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:25,560
Ah... / Ah...

25
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:27,260
As we all know.

26
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:38,260
EP.13 Spite

27
00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:41,380
P'Dan must be a really good mentor.

28
00:02:41,380 --> 00:02:43,120
That's why Pond finished his project so fast.

29
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:45,040
I don't even know if I'll make it in time.

30
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:49,960
Hey, girl, why would you say that?

31
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:53,240
Does that mean the mentor on this side

32
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:55,520
isn't taking good care of you?

33
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:59,480
Not at all! P'O is the absolute best.

34
00:02:59,480 --> 00:03:01,580
I'm just a slow learner myself.

35
00:03:01,580 --> 00:03:03,660
Even though I work hard,

36
00:03:03,660 --> 00:03:05,720
the more I do, the more stressed I get.

37
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:09,140
Don't stress out. Working while stressed only makes things worse.

38
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:11,480
Oh, wow.

39
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:12,840
Alright, alright.

40
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:15,900
This side has already spoken.

41
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:20,000
Does the other side have anything to say to the intern?

42
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:23,900
Honestly, I don't really know what to say.

43
00:03:23,900 --> 00:03:27,600
When it comes to interns, I think it's better to let the mentor speak.

44
00:03:28,300 --> 00:03:29,280
Dan,

45
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:30,900
say something on my behalf.

46
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:49,220
Um...

47
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:51,880
Honestly, I don't really know what to say either.

48
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,880
If you really want me to speak...

49
00:04:09,760 --> 00:04:10,860
Pond,

50
00:04:10,860 --> 00:04:13,600
Pond is a very talented intern,

51
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:15,860
and he's truly adorable.

52
00:04:16,460 --> 00:04:18,140
I just want to say thank you.

53
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:21,140
You don't have to force yourself.

54
00:04:21,140 --> 00:04:22,780
I'm not that adorable.

55
00:04:23,280 --> 00:04:24,940
You've always been adorable to me.

56
00:04:27,060 --> 00:04:28,500
Well,

57
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:31,140
do you have anything you want to say to us, Pond?

58
00:04:35,460 --> 00:04:37,860
I'd like to thank everyone

59
00:04:38,300 --> 00:04:39,980
for teaching me.

60
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,960
I will remember everything

61
00:04:42,480 --> 00:04:44,860
and use it for my clear future.

62
00:04:45,180 --> 00:04:46,840
That's all from me.

63
00:04:57,160 --> 00:04:58,780
Whoa, Dan...

64
00:04:58,780 --> 00:05:00,680
Drinking like this, will you even make it home?

65
00:05:01,900 --> 00:05:07,160
Oh, Tang-Oh! Are you here to take Dan home?

66
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:11,220
No way! I won't leave before midnight.

67
00:05:12,760 --> 00:05:15,360
Not at all. I'm joining in for a drink.

68
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:18,120
Oh, please, take a seat!

69
00:05:18,120 --> 00:05:19,600
Hey, Best, scoot over.

70
00:05:19,940 --> 00:05:21,560
I want to sit next to Dan.

71
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:22,320
You want to sit next to Dan?

72
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:23,520
Yeah, move over.

73
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:26,360
Alright, alright, look,

74
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:27,400
we can all sit together.

75
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:28,700
Yeah, sit down.

76
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:32,920
What brings you here?

77
00:05:33,520 --> 00:05:35,180
You startled me.

78
00:05:35,180 --> 00:05:38,020
What's with that look? You look like you've seen a ghost.

79
00:05:45,900 --> 00:05:47,200
Pond,

80
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:48,500
when are you heading back to Phrae?

81
00:05:50,340 --> 00:05:53,080
Did your friend tell you to chase me away?

82
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,300
Do you have any idea

83
00:05:55,300 --> 00:05:56,960
how mad P'Dan is at you?

84
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:00,220
Mad at me?

85
00:06:00,220 --> 00:06:01,460
What is he mad at me for?

86
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:05,420
Your friend was the one who packed his things and left the room

87
00:06:05,420 --> 00:06:07,680
without saying a single word to me.

88
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:08,700
Why should he be mad at me?

89
00:06:10,180 --> 00:06:12,960
He's mad because you called him easy!

90
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:16,000
Well, he is easy.

91
00:06:16,540 --> 00:06:18,200
He dumps me easily,

92
00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:19,640
he kicks me out easily,

93
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:23,120
and getting together with that friend...

94
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:24,600
That was pretty damn easy too.

95
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:29,700
Honestly, someone like you shouldn't have trouble finding someone new.

96
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:32,880
From what I've seen,

97
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:35,000
things are going pretty well with Kaen.

98
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:38,560
Your friend is the only one who thinks that way.

99
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:42,280
*Sigh*

100
00:06:43,900 --> 00:06:46,440
No wonder Tang-Oh said you're still a kid.

101
00:06:47,580 --> 00:06:48,520
Hey,

102
00:06:50,040 --> 00:06:51,340
yeah...

103
00:06:51,340 --> 00:06:54,460
Both of you need to listen to each other.

104
00:06:54,460 --> 00:06:56,200
Stop acting out of spite.

105
00:06:56,740 --> 00:06:58,720
You think I'm doing this out of spite?

106
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:00,560
Your friend—

107
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:02,440
whatever he tells me to do, I do it.

108
00:07:02,980 --> 00:07:04,520
Just like when you told P'Ton

109
00:07:04,520 --> 00:07:06,120
to keep his distance.

110
00:07:06,620 --> 00:07:08,520
P'Ton kept his distance too, didn't he?

111
00:07:14,360 --> 00:07:15,240
That's right.

112
00:07:15,860 --> 00:07:17,500
You told me to back off, so I did.

113
00:07:17,500 --> 00:07:19,040
And how did that work out?

114
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:21,380
Are you really happy now?

115
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:24,000
Ton...

116
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:24,720
Oh, right.

117
00:07:24,720 --> 00:07:26,360
I almost forgot.

118
00:07:26,360 --> 00:07:27,820
You don't want to talk to me.

119
00:07:28,500 --> 00:07:30,900
Ton, it's not like that.

120
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:32,260
Let's head outside, Pond.

121
00:07:32,260 --> 00:07:33,680
It's no fun here anymore.

122
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:34,580
Yeah.

123
00:07:34,580 --> 00:07:36,080
Let's get out of here.

124
00:07:54,460 --> 00:07:55,640
Dan,

125
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:58,360
are you really okay?

126
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:01,500
If you're not okay,

127
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:03,020
just tell me.

128
00:08:03,020 --> 00:08:04,980
I can go talk to him for you.

129
00:08:05,900 --> 00:08:07,220
Yeah... I'm okay.

130
00:08:07,220 --> 00:08:08,540
You don't need to do that.

131
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:10,720
Don't lie to me.

132
00:08:10,720 --> 00:08:12,580
You're a mess,

133
00:08:12,580 --> 00:08:14,260
and Best is a mess too.

134
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:19,360
So, how is Best doing?

135
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:21,960
Are you sure

136
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:23,460
you really want to know about him?

137
00:08:28,860 --> 00:08:29,980
Well,

138
00:08:29,980 --> 00:08:30,960
I'm heading back.

139
00:08:31,780 --> 00:08:32,440
Hey,

140
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:36,400
can you really stay alone?

141
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:38,580
Want me to keep you company?

142
00:08:38,580 --> 00:08:39,500
No need.

143
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:40,660
I'll be fine.

144
00:08:49,760 --> 00:08:51,440
Oh,

145
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:53,000
check this out.

146
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,940
Best says

147
00:08:55,940 --> 00:08:57,880
your boy is with his boy,

148
00:08:57,880 --> 00:08:59,560
and they're going for another round.

149
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:02,160
His boy?

150
00:09:03,800 --> 00:09:05,560
Yeah, Best's boy.

151
00:09:07,520 --> 00:09:09,000
Oh.

152
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,080
I see.

153
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:14,980
So... does this

154
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:16,980
make you feel any better?

155
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:20,940
Yeah.

156
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:23,820
Good.

157
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:24,760
Then,

158
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:27,260
I'll head back now.

159
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:29,060
Leaving already?

160
00:09:29,060 --> 00:09:29,940
Yeah.

161
00:10:01,640 --> 00:10:02,460
Hello?

162
00:10:02,460 --> 00:10:03,820
Hello?

163
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:05,180
P'Dan...

164
00:10:05,640 --> 00:10:07,520
Your friend is so cruel.

165
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:09,020
The absolute cruelest!

166
00:10:09,020 --> 00:10:10,900
He made me fall in love with him,

167
00:10:10,900 --> 00:10:12,520
and then he just ran off with someone else.

168
00:10:12,940 --> 00:10:14,820
Wait, calm down.

169
00:10:14,820 --> 00:10:16,180
Are you...

170
00:10:16,180 --> 00:10:17,180
Are you still at the same place?

171
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:20,780
I don't know where I am, P'...

172
00:10:20,780 --> 00:10:22,580
I'm all alone right now.

173
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:23,940
Hey,

174
00:10:24,440 --> 00:10:25,680
can you get home?

175
00:10:25,680 --> 00:10:26,840
I'm not going home.

176
00:10:27,180 --> 00:10:29,900
I'm going to lie in the middle of the street and let cars run me over!

177
00:10:30,220 --> 00:10:32,720
W-Wait! You can't lie down there!

178
00:10:32,940 --> 00:10:34,160
And where's...

179
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:36,040
Where's Best?

180
00:10:36,040 --> 00:10:37,560
I don't know!

181
00:10:37,560 --> 00:10:38,420
What about Pond?

182
00:10:39,040 --> 00:10:40,960
That jerk Pond went home already!

183
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:43,180
He abandoned me too, P'.

184
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:47,440
Wait, are you still at the same bar?

185
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:48,600
Share your location with me.

186
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:49,960
Share your location, I'll go pick you up.

187
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:51,600
I'll go pick you up!

188
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:54,920
Wait...

189
00:10:54,920 --> 00:10:56,300
Why did you hang up?

190
00:11:10,360 --> 00:11:12,240
Why aren't you picking up?

191
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:15,580
Hello?

192
00:11:15,580 --> 00:11:16,280
Where are you right now?

193
00:11:16,280 --> 00:11:18,200
Don't stand out in the rain!

194
00:11:20,560 --> 00:11:21,760
Too late, P'.

195
00:11:21,760 --> 00:11:23,700
I'm already soaked.

196
00:11:27,480 --> 00:11:28,980
Is that you, Pond?

197
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:31,460
Yeah.

198
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:34,280
Are you drunk?

199
00:11:34,620 --> 00:11:36,920
Do you actually care about me?

200
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,260
Where are you?

201
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:44,060
I don't know.

202
00:11:46,260 --> 00:11:48,040
Look around carefully. Where are you?

203
00:11:52,260 --> 00:11:54,460
In front of your room, I think.

204
